    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13450" root="دول" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَالٌ</span></b>  <i>One of the letters of the alphabet,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">د</span>,) <i>the
place of utterance of which is near to that of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span>:
masc. and fem.; so that you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَالٌ حَسَنٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَسَنَةٌ</span> [<i>a beautiful</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">د</span>]: the pl. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدْوَالٌ</span> if masc.,
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَالَاتٌ</span> [if fem.; the latter the more common].
(TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also A <i>fat</i> woman. (Kh, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَالَةٌ</span>.

